branch: feature/frame-language-tag-fallback

why: BACKLOG frame-language-with-grammatical-gender: `Slot.ask` is keyed
  by a language CODE, and a language whose question differs by the
  addressee's grammatical gender (Polish Pan/Pani, formal registers)
  needs more than a code -- or needs the caller to key by "pl-formal-f"
  and own the choice. The library should not model gender; it should
  let the caller key by the tag it owns and never quietly ask in the
  wrong language: `question("pl-formal-f")` finds that key, else "pl",
  else the fallback; `speaks` the same way. Laws in okay-frame; the
  entry closes with the rule written down.
